course: dictionary
lesson: 6205
title: Missing: lost, or not there
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. Missing is a good example. Look at the words around it, then ask: what fits here? «Ten pages were missing from the book.» Pages cannot be lost and still be in the book, so missing means not there, or lost.
explain: Missing can be an adjective, a word that describes a noun. It can also be the -ing form of the verb miss. «The striker kept missing the goal.» Here missing means not hitting. When you see a word ending in -ing after a verb like kept or keep, check whether it is an action.
explain: Missing can also mean feeling sad that someone is away: «I am missing you already.» Try your meaning in the sentence. If you swap in a meaning and the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Missing means not there, lost, or not yet found.
fact: «Missing» can also be the -ing form of «miss», as in «missing the bus», which means not catching it.
fact: «A missing person or pet» is one that is lost, and people are looking for it.
fact: «Fill in the missing word» means add the word that is not there yet.
fact: «Missing you» means feeling sad because someone is away.
exercise: «Ten pages were missing from the book.» What does missing mean here? | Very large | Read aloud | *Not there, lost | Shouting loudly
exercise: Editing can add «a missing sentence» to a story. What is a missing sentence? | A sentence that is too long | A sentence that was read aloud | *A sentence that is not there yet | A sentence in a different language
exercise: What does missing mean in «the striker kept missing the goal»? | Very tall | *Not hitting, as in a shot that goes wide | Found again | Not hitting
test: Reading your work aloud helps you hear what? | The title of the book | Nothing new | Only the pictures | *Missing words, clumsy sentences and tense slips
test: «A missing pet» is one that is what? | *Lost, and people are looking for it | Very quick | Asleep in the garden | Happy at home
exam: Which sentence uses missing to mean sad that someone is away? | «The missing number is seven.» | «Ten pages were missing from the book.» | *«I am missing you already.» | «The missing page was found under the sofa.»
